{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1462706-permanently-tainted-areas-in-europe","id":1462706,"title":"Permanently tainted areas in Europe","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-04T13:42:44-07:00","id":1462706,"title":"Permanently tainted areas in Europe","content":"Hello there,<br /> <br /> I'm running a monotribe white howler campain and I currently have 2 opportunities for my player to find ancestors. One is the wraith Cororuc, and the other one is Eubh the Ever-Living.<br /> <br /> Focusing on Eubh, I made him disappear after fighting the Narlthus to end the long winter, so a while ago. He succeeded not because he won, but because they got caught up in the ice until nowadays (I used some part of the Rite of Passage scenario). The BSD are unearthing the giant permafrost ice-coffin and the players want to stop that and take control of the area and find a way to free Eubh without freeing the Narlthus.<br /> <br /> If they succeed, what could be their options to clean the area, and what to with what they cannot clean ? I've of course thought of the Bane Tenders (even though for now they have 0 knowledge about Uktena's childrens and about American\u2019s Tribes as a whole, it\u2019s very EU centered right now) but I was wondering if anyone had any other interesting ideas.--<br /> --&gt; For me as long as the Narlthus is here there's no way that the area can be &quot;cleaned&quot; and it will have to be buried again if they don't want their beloved Scotland to have a second long winter<br /> <br /> As an interesting point of note there is another area White Howler related that nobody managed to clean completely from it's taint, the Mile-deep loch caern. So, what apply to one could be used for the other (or not). Both area are not related but that doesn\u2019t mean that a link couldn\u2019t exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T12:27:23-07:00","id":1462823,"title":"","content":"If I understand correctly, Eubh (is that a canon character or one you created?) fulfills the role of the Wendigo Theurge She-Cries-Ice in the published version of Rite of Passage. You just changed things to reset the the adventure in Scotland.<br /> <br /> First, it's totally fine for the area to remain tainted as a result of Narlthus being imprisoned. It just becomes an issue of the Garou needing to mow the lawn by eliminating Banes and Wyrm creatures attracted there, and to continually monitor the area. After all, that's what the earliest Garou must have done for thousands of years, and if it was normal to permanently cleanse it, they would have already done it. But that may not be what you want as an ST.<br /> <br /> Second, if you do want to eliminate the taint, you likely need some kind of special plot coupon that allows the Garou to eliminate or banish Narlthus. That plot coupon isn't normally available so you need to not only create its flavor text but explain why it's now possible for the Garou (in the form of the PCs) to get it for the first time. Since the original story stated Narlthus was such an anathema to Gaia that nothing related to her could contain it, so a meteor (something not of Gaia) was used to be its prison. So an obvious thing is that the meteor that fell to Earth was only part of a greater meteoride. That other half of the object has been circling the Earth in orbit for the past several thousand years - we can say it was collecting the spiritual energy of Helios that would allow it to destroy or banish Narlthus. Now that it has done its job, it'll enter the atmosphere and land on earth. The PCs just need to learn about this, find it, retrieve it, and then reperform the original rite that was used to defeat Narlthus. So you may want to cobble together different evidence from the original legend concerning Narlthus, new prophecies, and anything special the PCs learn or discover on their own. Once Narlthus is removed, then ordinary means of cleansing the land could be done.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are lots of other clever ideas that can justify the same, but that's what immediately springs to my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T04:37:44-07:00","id":1462882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1462706-permanently-tainted-areas-in-europe?p=1462823#post1462823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I understand correctly, Eubh (is that a canon character or one you created?) fulfills the role of the Wendigo Theurge She-Cries-Ice in the published version of Rite of Passage. You just changed things to reset the the adventure in Scotland.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eubh is indeed a canon character from the white howler book, and in my story he would have been the one stopping the Narlthus in the past. I kept the wolf spirit associated to him a spirit associated to death, and ghost. By consuming ancestor spirits (so it have a cost) willing to sacrifice themselves, she would be able to bring him back to life, hence the name, the Ever-living. (that's my interpretation of Eubh story).<br /> <br /> In my setting the long winter came from the Narlthus who arrived on earth using the same meteorite way and started to spread this new &quot;ice-age&quot;. The meteorite used to hide the Narlthus at the time was coming from Turog (Now destroyed and appears as Rorg - Rage across the heavens p43 &amp; 73). <br /> <br /> The legend was passed down by a Gurahl family that were keeping the land and that's how the players heard about it. (They have the rough ideas but not very precise details)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1462706-permanently-tainted-areas-in-europe?p=1462823#post1462823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So an obvious thing is that the meteor that fell to Earth was only part of a greater meteoride. That other half of the object has been circling the Earth in orbit for the past several thousand years - we can say it was collecting the spiritual energy of Helios that would allow it to destroy or banish Narlthus. Now that it has done its job, it'll enter the atmosphere and land on earth. The PCs just need to learn about this, find it, retrieve it, and then reperform the original rite that was used to defeat Narlthus. So you may want to cobble together different evidence from the original legend concerning Narlthus, new prophecies, and anything special the PCs learn or discover on their own. Once Narlthus is removed, then ordinary means of cleansing the land could be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea that a place where a Wyrm fang is imprisoned cannot be totally cleaned, it's such a huge threat I feel like it have to have consequences and put some pressure on it's keepers. I wanted to connect the players to Rorg (so they can bring him back to favor the White Howler) &amp; Helios so I really like the idea that the player would need the same materials (metorite and such).<br /> <br /> I can keep this idea but since the players will want to deliver Eubh without freeing the Wyrm Spirit they will need to proceed to a ritual to renew the Narlthus prison, allowing Eubh to be freed and &quot;resurrected&quot; thanks to the wolf that they will find along the way (they already have hints toward that). The resurrection may be another complication since they no longer have ancestor spirits so maybe a PC sacrificing his character to allow the tribe to get one of it's most eminent warrior back to teach them the white howler way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}